  "verbalization": "Trigowiin A is implicated in the target pathway leading to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple independent routes. The evidence suggests that Trigowiin A acts as a target for ME-180 and Sophoranochromene, both of which are themselves targets of other compounds. This indicates a potential mechanism where Trigowiin A may interact with these compounds, which in turn target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex suggests a possible role for Trigowiin A in modulating the activity of these targets, possibly through a shared or indirect interaction. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, emphasizing the importance of understanding how Trigowiin A influences the downstream signaling pathways involving EZH2/SUZ12/EED.",
